<Article title="About Embedded Engineering Toolkit" description="Why this independent collection of transparent embedded engineering calculators exists." eyebrow="About"><h2>A practical reference, not a black box</h2><p>Embedded Engineering Toolkit helps students, firmware developers, electronics engineers, and makers turn common interface and timer formulas into quick, reviewable calculations. Each tool keeps the equation close to the result and explains what is—and is not—included.</p><h2>Editorial approach</h2><p>Content is written in plain technical English, checked against the stated formulas, and designed to teach the reasoning behind each input. We do not invent credentials, endorsements, usage figures, or laboratory precision. When a result is an estimate, it is labeled as one.</p><h2>Privacy and sustainability</h2><p>Calculators run locally in the browser and currently require no account or database. The site may later support itself with clearly separated advertising, but advertising must not obstruct the engineering workflow.</p><h2>Feedback</h2><p>If an assumption is unclear or a calculation needs another documented mode, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Include the device family, expected result, and a reproducible input set.</p></Article>
